A||N||12||Jonathan||I DID trade Fiero for MR2||||13||
Z||000000||Jonathan||09-16-2000||12:00 AM||||I actually did do this in 1994.  I traded my black 86SE V6 (seen in signature) in on a 1991 Toyota Mr2, (Non-turbo, T-tops, etc)  I had several love/hates with the car.  <P>Loves:<P>More modern interior than the Fiero<BR>Super fast popup headlights<BR>Fun to drive spiritedly<BR>Position of the handbrake.  (Very good for helping suicide/bootleg turns)<BR>Decent styling<P>Hates:<P>1.  Sewing machine sounding engine.  <BR>2.  Red paint faded way too easily.  Could not get it buffed back the way I wanted it!<BR>3.  Could not work on engine easily.  Two different decklids, one for engine, one for trunk.  <BR>4.  THE REASON I SOLD IT...I could NEVER adjust the drivers seat to fit me comfortably.<P>I should say, I really enjoyed this car.  BUT, It just wasn't the same!!!  I missed my Fiero soon after I traded it.  I sold the MR2 after owning it for 6 months.  I bought a New Grand Am GT, and then two Fieros!!<P>I might have kept it had it not been for the seat problem.  But, I would have bought another Fiero ANYWAY!!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotag2.jpg"> ||||reg||13
