Z||000002||DjKid||09-16-2000||02:32 PM||||I'll say its a nice car, not that bad lookin... I wouldn't mind having one but I'd take a fiero over a mr2 anyday. can't help I like my homegrown cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Dun like Pontiac though, Love muh Fiero!!!!!!!!!!!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jonathan||09-16-2000||03:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>So, what your saying is you disagree with all the people who say they get sick when they see an MR2, and you agree it is a really nice, peppy car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I did enjoy the car.  Just not as much as my Fiero.  If I had the money, I might own both still.  But having to choose, I chose the <B>Fiero!</B> <BR>The car is fairly quick too.  I smoked my friend's 92 Camaro V6 so often that he finally got tired of racing.  <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotag2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
